 ——————— FORBIDDEN Chaos By Design US Tour 2026 Godfathers in
  the Bay Area metal scene\, Forbidden have returned with their first album
  in 16 years to unleash 12 fierce\, uncompromising\, and supremely progres
 sive songs which signal an almighty return. Forbidden will be released by 
 BLKIIBLK Records and charts a defiant journey through scything riffs\, inc
 redible melodies\, 24 karat lead guitars\, simply thunderous drums and bas
 s\, plus the studio debut of Norman Skinner (Niviane & Imagika) whose soar
 ing vocals elevate the material to unprecedented levels. Conceived by foun
 der and guitarist Craig Locicero alongside his creative brother\, drummer 
 Chris Kontos\, the foundational energy of bassist Matt Camacho\, the versa
 tility and poise of guitarist Jeremy Von Epp\, and Skinner’s voracious f
 resh approach\, Forbidden sees the band arriving at their finest hour with
  their richest-ever line-up. With Skinner stepping up to take on lyrical d
 uties\, Forbidden takes a fierce and uncompromising look into the eyes of 
 our times without taking sides\, instead imploring people to recognize the
  false conflicts created by the current society and how they can conquer a
 nd rise above them. Take the blistering roar of “Single Point Failure”
 \, the beautiful orchestral savagery of “Flower of Life”\, and the rel
 entless charge of “Burning The Lungs Of Earth.” There’s also the mid
 -paced brooding power of “Psyclops\,” the twisting\, winding power for
 ce of “Sycophantasy” featuring guest vocals from Mastodon’s Brann Da
 ilor\, and a thunderous ode to women “The Burden” featuring guest voca
 ls from Kayla Dixon. In addition\, Forbidden pay homage to classic America
 n heavy metal band\, Savatage in the shape of a malevolent and mesmeric co
 ver of “Sirens”\, which embraces Greek mythology. Recorded\, produced 
 and engineered at Sharkbite Studios in Oakland\, California with engineer 
 and co-producer Zack Ohren\, Forbidden is the the resounding realization o
 f a band which has finally found inner-peace\, and furious cohesion\, in e
 xpressing its true passionate angst and incredible metal heart. Check out 
 Forbidden here! Website | Instagram | Facebook Supported By: Heathen\, Voi
